# Build context trim for `docker build -f docker/Dockerfile .` (root context, whole reactor).
#
# docker/Dockerfile deliberately does `COPY . .` rather than listing modules: the reactor builds
# `service`'s dependencies on `qits-workspaces-domain` and `qits-workspaces-daemon-protocol` from
# source (neither is published), and a module list would have to be edited every time a module is
# added. This file is what makes that cheap — it drops everything the build does not need, so adding
# a module stays free and no stale output leaks in.

.git
.gitignore

# Maven / Quarkus build output — regenerated inside the build stage, and by far the bulk of a working
# tree here (three modules' target/, one holding a native binary and its build artifacts). Copying it
# in would also risk a stale target/ shadowing what the stage compiles.
**/target
**/target-ide

# Agent scratch, and the one entry the sibling repos do not carry: `.claude/worktrees/` holds full
# checkouts of this repo, each with its own target/. Untracked and machine-local, so it is invisible
# in a diff and unbounded in size — without this line the context is dominated by copies of the very
# sources being built.
.claude

# Local env / IDE cruft
.env
.idea
.vscode
.sdkmanrc

# Docs and the docker/ dir itself: nothing in the build reads them, and keeping them out means
# editing this Dockerfile or a README does not bust the `COPY . .` layer.
*.md
docs
docker
